# **Order Queue — UX Decisions (May 28, 2026)**

## Desktop: Kanban Board

Replaced the tab-per-status layout with a Jira-style 4-lane kanban board. All orders visible simultaneously across all statuses -- no tab switching during a rush.

**Lanes:** New / In Progress / Ready / Picked Up

**Card format:** `#42 · Sandy · Chocolate Ice Cream` -- order number, customer name, first item (truncated if multiple). Time elapsed shown below. Color-coded by lane.

**Two buttons per card:**
- **View** -- opens modal with full order detail (all items, special request, total, time)
- **Move →** -- advances to next status immediately, no modal, no confirmation. Label changes per lane: "Start →" / "Ready →" / "Picked Up →"

**Picked Up lane:** View only. No Move button. Cards dimmed.

**Modal:** Full item list, special request, total, SMS confirmation status. Action button advances status. Cancel order button on New and In Progress modals only. Back-step available: Ready → In Progress only (not back to New).

**One-tap Pause** always visible in page header. **Walk-up (＋)** button always visible for manual orders.

## Mobile: Tab Strip + Inline Expand

Tab strip (New / In Progress / Ready / Picked Up) with live badge counts. New tab badge is red, In Progress is amber, Ready is green.

**Card format:** Order number (large) + name only. No item detail on collapsed card.

**Single tap** -- expands card inline with full order detail + action button to advance. Other cards remain visible and scrollable above and below.

**Double-tap** -- advances to next status directly, no modal, no confirmation. Fast path for experienced owners during rush.

**New order banner** pulses at top when a new order arrives. Push notification fires to locked screen with order number, name, items, total.

## Wireframe Reference

QOA_Queue_Wireframe.html -- separate focused file covering desktop kanban and 4 mobile states.

# **Open UX Questions — Queue**

- Queue UX is functional but not yet fully optimized. Need to continue exploring flows that minimize taps and clicks for high-volume rush scenarios. Ideas to explore: swipe gestures on mobile cards to advance status, keyboard shortcuts on desktop, batch-advance (select multiple New orders and start all at once), audio cue differentiation by status (different sounds for New vs Ready pickup).

- Double-tap on mobile for status advance: needs usability validation. Could be hard to discover. Consider a brief onboarding tooltip or a "quick actions" long-press menu as alternative.

- Should the kanban board auto-scroll or highlight cards that have been waiting too long (e.g., card border pulses red after N minutes in New)?

- Picked Up lane: show last N orders only, or collapse to a count? Infinite scroll adds clutter.

- Walk-up orders on mobile: currently only accessible from desktop header. Needs a mobile entry point.
